<title>UK: B.A.T gains after Morris shares rise.</title>
<headline>B.A.T gains after Morris shares rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries Plc rose in early trading on Tuesday, echoing a sharp rise in shares in U.S. tobacco company Philip Morris Cos Inc, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 7-1/2p at 540-1/2 by 0817 GMT. Morris shares closed $6-1/8 higher at $135-1/8 yesterday, helping power a rally in the blue-chip Dow index.</p>
<p>Tobacco stocks have been boosted in the past month by prospects for a settlement in the growing number of legal claims in the U.S. over smoking-related diseases.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
